{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544831-signature-characters","id":1544831,"title":"Signature Characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-26T21:22:02-07:00","id":1544831,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Signature Characters","content":"This was something that crossed my mind later and also based on<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25666\" data-vbnamecard=\"25666\">Illuminostro</a> comment in another thread. Basically, each clan has a signature character that, at least in theory, should represent the clan. So I come to ask, what do you think each of these characters should be like? Note that I'm not necessarily asking what you think of the existing signature characters, although that would also be a valid answer, but rather what you think a clan signature character should be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T00:29:33-07:00","id":1544833,"title":"","content":"The quintessential Follower of Set in my eyes is <b>Andreas Aegyptus/Ankhesenaten</b> from the Dark Ages Clan Novel 4: Setite<br /> He really what and how his clan should be portrayed - a merchant, a devoted beliver, a Lector Priest, a corruptor and converter and his relationship with his ghouls really mirrors the realtionship of his clan with theirs in my humble opinion<br /> <br /> For the Tzimsice it would be <b>Danika Ruthven </b>from Lair of the Hidden<br /> She is the master of her domain, a charming but cold host, well versed in Koldunic sorcery and Vicissitude and long ago abandnoned the views of humanity to become something more (even tho' she is on the path for Golconda - I don't think she walked the Unmapped Road to become Human again but to transcende what she is now - a very metamorphosist view) and I think she not really considered Nikanuuranu, the Earthbound of the Neberu Cretheus summoned a &quot;Demon&quot; but a Kupala-like entity (she might be right in that one), something her Clan was intimitaely familiar with and belived like with the &quot;lesser kupalas&quot; she can handle it<br /> The other candidate for Tzimisce Signature Character would be <b>Strahd von Zarovich</b> or Lady <b>Alcina Dimitrescu</b><br /> <br /> The Ventrue Signature Character would be either <b>Mithras </b>before (or actually even after) diablerie or eeither <b>Dracula</b> portrayed by Gary Oldman from Francis Ford Coppola's Bram Stoker's Dracula<br /> <br /> The Malkavian would be <b>Hannibal Lecter</b> - insane but totally functinal in society and dangerous or <b>Bruce Wayne</b>, insanse with a very dangerous alternate personality (the Joker would be a Sabbat Malkavian) at the verge of imploding<br /> <br /> The Gangrel would be <b>Cuthbert Beckett</b><br /> <br /> The Toreador would be <b>Velvet Velour</b> from Bloodlines<br /> <br /> The Brujah? <b>Lucifer </b>from Paradise Lost by John Milton or from the TV series Lucifer Morningstar; both are the quintessential Brujah<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu would be <b>Pearl </b>from Blade movie<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim would be <b>Ghost Dog </b>from the 1999 movie Ghost Dog: The Way of the Samurai<br /> <br /> The Lasombra would be <b>Leto Atreides</b> the Second from Children of Dune; ruthless, determined and not afraid to use something totally alien and unknown to rule, he is an elegent predator of Humanity (altho with good intentions) <b>Baron Harkonnen</b> is a close second candidate<br /> <br /> The Ravnos is really depend of the indian or europen branch but I think t<b>he Count of Monte Cristo </b>is what a Ravnos deep down is<br /> <br /> The Giovanni...<b> Boris Balkan</b> from the 1999 horror movie The Ninth Gate<br /> <br /> The Tremere , don't laugh, but <b>Severus Snape</b>. Cold, calculating, precise, sarcastic, and bitter, no one realyl likes him but they keep him around and <i>tolerate</i> him (and his very dark past) for his knowledge and services<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-27-2024, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T05:20:57-07:00","id":1544837,"title":"","content":"The main issue with signature characters is that to be believable they have to fall within a certain range of behaviors and traits, but every clan and bloodline is intentionally designed to encompass a wide range of potential character types so that anyone can find something to play in that clan regardless of what they are into.<br /> <br /> When most people think &quot;artist&quot; they automatically think Toreador, but when most people think &quot;Toreador&quot; they think more along the lines of hedonists, socialites, artsy people who are looking for their next muse. To me, an artist is someone who refines their technique and understanding of their art rather than being distracted by living life. Consider the Dancer, Martial Artist, or the musician who practices for hours on end, only to be put in the same category as someone who is overly impressed with their own poetry.<br /> <br /> Another good example of the lack of focus is the average Malkavian. People see the word &quot;Insane&quot; and automatically think Malkavian, despite the word &quot;Insane&quot; being a legal term rather than a medical one in the modern world. A person who can't tell right from wrong is insane, but a person who knows right from wrong but does it anyway is sane. Thus the Jack the Ripper character from the Johnny Depp movie &quot;From Hell&quot; is more of a malkavian in my mind than say Hannibal Lector, who for the record always felt more like a Nagaraja to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T09:44:33-07:00","id":1544846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544831-signature-characters?p=1544837#post1544837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When most people think &quot;artist&quot; they automatically think Toreador, but when most people think &quot;Toreador&quot; they think more along the lines of hedonists, socialites, artsy people who are looking for their next muse. To me, an artist is someone who refines their technique and understanding of their art rather than being distracted by living life. Consider the Dancer, Martial Artist, or the musician who practices for hours on end, only to be put in the same category as someone who is overly impressed with their own poetry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I follow the more practical line of thought that art is anything that requires a technique that requires training. Which would include pretty much anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T13:23:58-07:00","id":1544915,"title":"","content":"I am not a fan of signature characters. They are a marketing tool and nothing more. They might be good, interesting characters, or cliched, bland characters in and of themselves, but in the end they are just a marketing tool. They exist so marketing and sourcebook writers can refer to standard copyrighted characters and build a brand. They might be good for that purpose, but I am uninterested in them.<br /> <br /> Clans do have archetypes, and we have lots of examples of characters who fit those archetypes. The various Players Guides and Clanbooks are filled with them generic concepts that can be easily customized and fit into most chronicles. I usually find the best city by night sourcebooks to have more compelling characters of the clans than any signature character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T10:51:14-07:00","id":1545055,"title":"","content":"Incredibly hot characters that the fans should make fan art and fanfic of to artificially generate content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-31T13:32:13-07:00","id":1545102,"title":"","content":"I agree that I found Kevin Jackson as the Prince in Chicago By Night quite interesting to see a older neonate being able to juggle the egos of kindred who are way older and more powerful then him quite compelling.<br /> <br /> As for Malkavians I keep thinking of Johnny Depp, Nicolas Cage or the late Billy Drago giving off the unearthly vibe that is the Moon Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-31-2024, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T21:07:36-08:00","id":1545431,"title":"","content":"Unrelated but kind of related - do any of the clan novels mention when did Aisling Sturbridge become &quot;chief-regent&quot; of New York?<br /> <br /> The info on <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aisling_Sturbridge\" target=\"_blank\">her</a> wiki entry and those of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ephraim_Wainwright\" target=\"_blank\">Ephraim</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eugenio_Estevez\" target=\"_blank\">Eugenio</a> is fragmentary (and contradicts itself at times - Eugenio's entry speaks of him coming with the idea of the multiple chantries as he participated along with Aisling in the preparations to retake New York, while all other entries seem to imply this is a holdover from Maupassant's besieged tenure during the Sabbat-dominated era.<br /> <br /> Anyway, kind of interested in what info there is in Aisling history between the disappearance of her sire and her assuming as top regent of New York around the time of the Polonia &amp; Vykos' american crusade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-06-2024, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T17:35:58-08:00","id":1545544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544831-signature-characters?p=1545431#post1545431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated but kind of related - do any of the clan novels mention when did Aisling Sturbridge become &quot;chief-regent&quot; of New York?<br /> <br /> The info on <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aisling_Sturbridge\" target=\"_blank\">her</a> wiki entry and those of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ephraim_Wainwright\" target=\"_blank\">Ephraim</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eugenio_Estevez\" target=\"_blank\">Eugenio</a> is fragmentary (and contradicts itself at times - Eugenio's entry speaks of him coming with the idea of the multiple chantries as he participated along with Aisling in the preparations to retake New York, while all other entries seem to imply this is a holdover from Maupassant's besieged tenure during the Sabbat-dominated era.<br /> <br /> Anyway, kind of interested in what info there is in Aisling history between the disappearance of her sire and her assuming as top regent of New York around the time of the Polonia &amp; Vykos' american crusade.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the second (1997) edition of <i>World of Darkness</i>, it is mentioned that Sturbridge is the Regent of <b>the</b> Tremere Chantry at Barnard College with no mention of any other chantries. I'd imagine it either happened shortly before or shortly after the Sabbat were kicked out. My other bit of speculation is that since Sturbridge was the head of the sole Chantry, putting someone above her would be insulting, given her ability to keep the chantry going despite being deep in Sabbat and Setite territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T19:52:28-08:00","id":1545547,"title":"","content":"You know Gillian Anderson would make a good Aisling Sturbridge or Terrance Stamp as her mysterious sire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T08:05:13-08:00","id":1545569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>higgipedia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544831-signature-characters?p=1545544#post1545544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the second (1997) edition of <i>World of Darkness</i>, it is mentioned that Sturbridge is the Regent of <b>the</b> Tremere Chantry at Barnard College with no mention of any other chantries. I'd imagine it either happened shortly before or shortly after the Sabbat were kicked out. My other bit of speculation is that since Sturbridge was the head of the sole Chantry, putting someone above her would be insulting, given her ability to keep the chantry going despite being deep in Sabbat and Setite territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, that kinds of creates more issues - but now i'm asking myself if the whole &quot;multiple autonomous but coordinated Tremere chantries&quot; conceit from NY by Night was not an attempt to patch up conflicting info from NPC write-ups on previous books (Sturbridge in '97 on WoD 2ed, and Wainwright in '00 on Nights of Prophecy).<br /> Guess i'll look into both books to compare, contrast and come up with my own take of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T15:00:12-08:00","id":1545585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544831-signature-characters?p=1545569#post1545569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm, that kinds of creates more issues - but now i'm asking myself if the whole &quot;multiple autonomous but coordinated Tremere chantries&quot; conceit from NY by Night was not an attempt to patch up conflicting info from NPC write-ups on previous books (Sturbridge in '97 on WoD 2ed, and Wainwright in '00 on Nights of Prophecy).<br /> Guess i'll look into both books to compare, contrast and come up with my own take of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Wait, mass quantities of interrelated books written by different freelancers have continuity issues? Perish the thought!&quot; he said sarcastically.<br /> <br /> I could easily see multiple chantries in the city, though. <b>MY</b> New York in the WoD has about 400 Kindred in the five boroughs, about 30 being Tremere. But, a big theme in my game is that New York is too big for any Kindred to control effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-09T15:57:36-08:00","id":1545625,"title":"","content":"400 Kindred is quite a sizeable amount in for a city of 8 million higgipedia. Is the Prince really powerful in terms of allies or enforcement to keep things from bubbling over and risking the Masquerade. We thought we were pushing it with 30 or so in Calgary where the population is just over a million and is mainly a Anarch fiefdom and the eldest members have a loose agreement of what regions are safe to feed from and whom the local lord or lady is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T18:29:30-08:00","id":1545721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544831-signature-characters?p=1545625#post1545625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">400 Kindred is quite a sizeable amount in for a city of 8 million higgipedia. Is the Prince really powerful in terms of allies or enforcement to keep things from bubbling over and risking the Masquerade. We thought we were pushing it with 30 or so in Calgary where the population is just over a million and is mainly a Anarch fiefdom and the eldest members have a loose agreement of what regions are safe to feed from and whom the local lord or lady is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's roughly 1:21,000, so five times the &quot;norm.&quot; I arrived at this decision based on a combination of conceits. First, New York is so big and so dense that it attracts more Kindred as there are so many moving parts, it can be easy for any authority to lose track of other Kindred. And while a New York of 2024 is gentrified enough that I think it would be hard to support a population that high, my WOD NYC is much more along the lines of the 1970s &quot;Fear City&quot; New York. LOTS of places to hide and no-mans-lands where it is hard for Camarilla to get eyes and project power.<br /> <br /> Another factor in my games is that more than half of those 400 are either fledglings created within the last 15 years or 13th Generation (a substantial part of that number are both). Also, roughly one third of the population are not part of either the Camarilla or Anarchs. All of those things really contribute to an overflow vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T18:53:11-08:00","id":1545724,"title":"","content":"Same here most of the Kindred in Calgary in our game are of the 12th-13th generation with a couple of members of the 9th generation and most of the ancillae being largely of the 11th and one or two members of the 10th generation. Not to many Thin Bloods yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}